# 1. Purpose and Scope

This document specifies the functional requirements for the Workforce Planning module of the OPEX Budgeting System (OBS). It defines what the system must do — the business rules, data rules, access control behaviours, and acceptance criteria that govern position management, compensation calculations, employee lifecycle events, the transfer workflow, and the derivation of personnel expense budget lines in the Budget Planning module.

This specification resolves the following open items from predecessor documents:

- Budget Planning Functional Requirements v1.1, Section 1.2 — Workforce Planning functional requirements noted as covered in a separate pending specification.

- UX and UI Specification v1.5, Sections 6.1–6.5 — Workforce Planning UI behaviour defined; this document adds the underlying functional and data rules.

- Application Architecture Specification v3.6, Section 3.3 — Calculation service compensation burden and merit increase rules flagged for Workforce Planning specification. Amendment issued — rules now defined in this document.

- Domain Glossary v1.9 — Merit increase definition amended: the global Administrator-configured rate supersedes any per-cost-center owner configuration reference.

All architectural decisions recorded in the Application Architecture Specification v3.6, Security and Access Control Specification v1.4, UX and UI Specification v1.5, Data Integration Specification v1.6, and Budget Planning Functional Requirements v1.1 are final and are not re-litigated here. This document adds functional detail on top of those decisions without contradicting them.

## 1.1 In Scope

- Position management — adding open positions, viewing filled positions imported from the HR admin system.

- Compensation data — base salary, merit increase, salary adjustment, AIPEIP bonus, other bonus, and compensation burden rate calculations.

- Merit increase configuration — global Administrator-configured rate applied to all positions.

- Compensation burden rate configuration — Administrator-configured rates per fiscal year, including salary cap handling for FICA and unemployment tax components.

- Compensation component to expense account mapping — system-level Administrator-configured mapping table.

- Employee lifecycle events — salary adjustment, termination, and retirement with proration rules.

- Transfer workflow — cross-cost-center position transfer with designated approver, expiry, and notification.

- Personnel expense derivation — direct push of Workforce Planning calculations to Budget Planning personnel expense budget lines.

- Headcount derivation for overhead allocation — budgeted headcount including filled and open positions.

- Administration module screens — merit increase rate, burden rates, salary caps, and compensation component mapping.

- PostgreSQL schema additions and API endpoint requirements for all of the above.

## 1.2 Out of Scope

- Finance-side approval workflow — fully specified in Functional Requirements: Finance Approval Workflow v1.2.

- Reporting functional requirements — covered in Functional Requirements: Reporting v1.1.

- HR admin system configuration — the HR system is a read-only data source for OBS. OBS does not write back to the HR system.

- Payroll processing — OBS produces budget figures only; it does not process or transmit payroll data.

- Benefits administration — burden rates represent the employer cost; individual employee benefit elections are not managed in OBS.

